<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Peronists get quorum for tax debate.</title>
<headline>Argentine Peronists get quorum for tax debate.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's ruling Peronist Party obtained a quorum Wednesday in the lower house of Congress to debate Economy Minister Roque Fernandez's tax package.</p>
<p>The Peronist government suffered a setback in Congress last Wednesday when it failed to muster a sufficient number of lawmakers in the lower house to debate the measures, which it hopes will help curb a looming $6.6 billion budget gap.</p>
<p>They needed a quorum of 130 to begin debate in the Chamber of Deputies.</p>
<p>-- Stephen Brown, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0695</p>
</text>
